.TH "CITADEL" "1" "Jul 2026" "AceTeam" "Citadel CLI Manual"

.SH NAME
citadel-attach - Attach to the running citadel worker on this node


.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBcitadel attach [flags]\fP


.SH DESCRIPTION
Discover the citadel worker already running on this node and show its
status, rather than starting a competing second process.

.PP
Docker-daemon style: a node runs exactly one worker, and everything else is a
client of it. 'citadel attach' names the running instance (PID, version, uptime)
and shows its live node identity, health, and managed services, read from the
worker's local status server.

.PP
If no worker is running, it says so and points you at 'citadel work'.

.PP
Use --shell to instead open an interactive shell on the running control center
(the TUI you launched with 'citadel'). Ctrl+] detaches; Ctrl-D exits the shell.


.SH OPTIONS
\fB-h\fP, \fB--help\fP[=false]
	help for attach

.PP
\fB--shell\fP[=false]
	Open an interactive shell on the running control center (instead of printing status). Ctrl+] detaches; Ctrl-D exits the shell.


.SH OPTIONS INHERITED FROM PARENT COMMANDS
\fB--debug\fP[=false]
	Enable debug output

.PP
\fB--no-auto-update\fP[=false]
	Disable automatic update checks and installs for this run (or set CITADEL_NO_AUTO_UPDATE=1)

.PP
\fB--no-color\fP[=false]
	Disable colorized output


.SH SEE ALSO
\fBcitadel(1)\fP
